Erik Hesselink wrote:
> 
> Beth Friedman wrote:
> 
> > I'd like to think that it's possible to get a decent wizard going
> > without having to depend on an early wish or a really good bones pile.
> > But that's the only way I've ever managed to ascend a wizard.

Getting a wizard started is hard.
> 
> * Use your pet, especially for the very low level monsters (level your
> pet, but they don't help you) and the very tough ones. Heal him if you can.

I try to leave the one XP monsters for my pet right from the
beginning, the newts, grid bugs and jackals. Wiz mode
suggests to me that your pet levels up based on number of
kills regardless of difficulty.

> * Engrave Elbereth if you're in a really tough spot, like the inevitable
> ants you mention.

Magicbane is great for this. A wand of digging, fire or
lightning is better saved for Elbereth until you have
Magicbane.

> * Use daggers. Advance your dagger skill as far as possible, and find a
> nice stack of daggers to throw.

Great advice. You get a +2 to hit which is a big deal to the
starting character. You can gain experience for advancing
the skill by throwing or melee. Have your pet check out one
and name it cursed or OK. If you can find a general store or
make it to Minetown have the shopkeeper tell you the
enchantment by offering to sell. (2z is 0 or negative, +5z
for every +1 enchantment.) Add that to the name. Future
daggers of similar enchantment and buc will stack! Throw
away that quarterstaff.

> * I usually go to Sokoban first.

If you have infravision or if the first level of the mines
is lit, the mines aren't too dangerous. You should try to do
one level for the armor and a pick ax even if all you have
is a lamp. 

Don't go around burdened. #e-test new wands. I think if you
can acquire Magicbane and get through Sokoban and the mines,
particularly if you find some means of reflection, you
should be a favorite to go all the way.

